{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1766777,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Innov-a-thon 2.0 2026 ","festival_id":null,"organization_id":947,"web_url":"www.instagram.com\/inno.nitr_official?stkn=MXFiOG03MnZnM2U3Yw==","start_date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-14T00:01:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/innov-a-thon-2026-nit-rourkela-1766777","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Innov-a-thon 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Innov-a-thon 2026<\/strong> is a problem-first innovation challenge organized by the <strong>Entrepreneurship Cell, NIT Rourkela<\/strong>, as part of <strong>Innovision Tech Fest 2026<\/strong>, NIT Rourkela&rsquo;s annual technical and innovation festival.<\/p>\n<p>The competition aims to encourage students to identify meaningful real-world problems, validate them through research, and develop innovative, scalable and impactful solutions.<\/p>\n<p>Unlike conventional hackathons that focus directly on building solutions, <strong>Innov-a-thon follows a problem-first approach<\/strong>, emphasizing problem discovery, user research, validation, ideation and solution development.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Event Format<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Problem Discovery &amp; Research<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>7 October 2026 &ndash; 31 October 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Participants will identify and validate a real-world problem and submit a <strong>Problem Definition Document (PDD)<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>The PDD should include:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clear problem statement<\/li>\n<li>User research and insights<\/li>\n<li>Market research and analysis<\/li>\n<li>Competitor landscape<\/li>\n<li>Validation evidence through surveys, interviews or relevant data<\/li>\n<li>Potential impact and target audience<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Submissions will be evaluated based on the <strong>clarity of the problem, depth of research, validation, significance and potential impact<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 Results<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>4 November 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will be announced on <strong>4 November 2026<\/strong> and will advance to Round 2.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Solution Development &amp; Pitch<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Starting 13 November 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will develop their proposed solutions and present their ideas before a panel of judges.<\/p>\n<p>Round 2 will focus on:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Solution development<\/li>\n<li>Innovation and feasibility<\/li>\n<li>Prototype\/MVP development<\/li>\n<li>Business model and scalability<\/li>\n<li>Potential impact<\/li>\n<li>Final presentation and pitch<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Innovision 2026 Campus Experience<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The <strong>Round 2 finalists will be invited to NIT Rourkela from 13&ndash;15 November 2026<\/strong> as part of <strong>Innovision Tech Fest 2026<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>Finalists will need to pay the applicable <strong>campus registration fee<\/strong>, which will include <strong>accommodation and food during the event<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>Beyond the competition, finalists will get the opportunity to experience the vibrant Innovision campus environment, including:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technical and innovation events<\/li>\n<li>Networking with students, entrepreneurs and industry professionals<\/li>\n<li>Exposure to a diverse community of innovators<\/li>\n<li>Fun activities and campus experiences<\/li>\n<li><strong>DJ nights and cultural events<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Opportunities to interact with participants from colleges across India<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>This makes Innov-a-thon more than just a competition&mdash;it is an opportunity to <strong>build, pitch, network and experience one of NIT Rourkela's biggest student festivals<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to undergraduate and postgraduate students from recognized institutions across India.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must provide valid and verifiable registration details.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are permitted.<\/li>\n<li>Students from different disciplines and specializations may form teams.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Team Size<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Minimum:<\/strong> 2 members<\/li>\n<li><strong>Maximum:<\/strong> 6 members<\/li>\n<li>A participant can be part of only one team.<\/li>\n<li>Multiple registrations by the same participant may lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Why Participate?<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Transform real-world problems into innovative solutions.<\/li>\n<li>Develop problem-solving, research and entrepreneurial skills.<\/li>\n<li>Receive mentorship and guidance from experienced professionals and entrepreneurs.<\/li>\n<li>Network with innovators and students from across India.<\/li>\n<li>Showcase your ideas before a panel of judges.<\/li>\n<li>Earn recognition through certificates and awards.<\/li>\n<li>Get the opportunity to experience <strong>Innovision Tech Fest 2026 at NIT Rourkela<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Connect with a wider ecosystem of innovators, entrepreneurs and industry professionals.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Code of Conduct<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Plagiarism and submission of pre-existing work without disclosure are prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must submit their own original work.<\/li>\n<li>Cheating, collusion or malpractice may result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must maintain professional and respectful conduct throughout the competition.<\/li>\n<li>Misconduct, harassment or disruption may result in removal from the competition.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the organizers and jury will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Organized By<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Entrepreneurship Cell, NIT Rourkela<\/strong><br \/><strong>As part of Innovision Tech Fest 2026, NIT Rourkela<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user